{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure","id":473605,"title":"Question about the pure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-08T18:57:18-07:00","id":473605,"title":"Question about the pure","content":"Hei guys,first things first,i must apologize for any grammar or spelling mistakes i may make,i'm from brazil,my english is not that good About The Pure. Do any of you Empathize with them?Or at Least feel a little sorry for them?Because i do. I'm not saying i think they are the good guys,or that what they do is right. they are monsters,but if you look at their story... They had a Home in Pangea,it was a paradise for them. They could whatever they pleased,hunt whatever they wanted,they were Happy.And they were with their father. And them,theyr brothers murdered their father and as a consequence,they lost their home,they lost everything. i dont know,maybe its just me,but i think i can see why they are angry,they lost their dad,they lost their home,no wonder they want payback","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:58:30-07:00","id":473714,"title":"","content":"Is this for Werewolf: The Apocalypse or Werewolf: The Forsaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:28:25-07:00","id":473785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=473714#post473714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this for Werewolf: The Apocalypse or Werewolf: The Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh,i forgot to specify. is for forsaken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T02:49:16-07:00","id":474018,"title":"","content":"So, you have clicked yourself into the wrong forum. Maybe an admin will move this topic to a place forsaken - or simply the Werewolf: The Forsaken section...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:08:11-07:00","id":475014,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Thread Moved to Forsaken subforum.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:16:38-07:00","id":475037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure#post473605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hei guys,first things first,i must apologize for any grammar or spelling mistakes i may make,i'm from brazil,my english is not that good About The Pure. Do any of you Empathize with them?Or at Least feel a little sorry for them?Because i do. I'm not saying i think they are the good guys,or that what they do is right. they are monsters,but if you look at their story... They had a Home in Pangea,it was a paradise for them. They could whatever they pleased,hunt whatever they wanted,they were Happy.And they were with their father. And them,theyr brothers murdered their father and as a consequence,they lost their home,they lost everything. i dont know,maybe its just me,but i think i can see why they are angry,they lost their dad,they lost their home,no wonder they want payback</div> </div> </div> </div> To deal with the OP's question, yes, but not because of what you said. The Firstborn who lead the Pure could have stopped the Five if they tried. Instead, they stood by, complained, and watched Daddy Wolf die without so much of a how-do-you-do, and then they claimed the Five were the wicked ones. No, my sympathy is with the Pure who are today, who are trapped by a event that happened aeons ago and slaves to mad spirits by their propaganda and their hatred. That, and I've always been paranoid that if I were a Uratha in-game, I'd probably end up being press-ganges into the Fire-Touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:29:31-07:00","id":475048,"title":"","content":"You can probably see a lot of views about how people play the Pure, whether they empathize with them or not, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes\">in this thread.</a><br /> <br /> And another thread about what 'we' the posters would prefer to be if we were in the World of Darkness and Uratha to boot <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be\">here.</a> Though this thread devolves into arguments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:28:15-07:00","id":475176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=475037#post475037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To deal with the OP's question, yes, but not because of what you said. The Firstborn who lead the Pure could have stopped the Five if they tried. Instead, they stood by, complained, and watched Daddy Wolf die without so much of a how-do-you-do, and then they claimed the Five were the wicked ones. No, my sympathy is with the Pure who are today, who are trapped by a event that happened aeons ago and slaves to mad spirits by their propaganda and their hatred. That, and I've always been paranoid that if I were a Uratha in-game, I'd probably end up being press-ganges into the Fire-Touched.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I feel the opposite. The Pure who were actually around before the fall are the ones I empathize with. Their siblings decided to commit patricide despite not all agreeing it was the best decision, yet they were all punished for it, even those who abstained. It makes sense that the members of the first pack who did not agree with that decision sought out like-minded Firstborn for patronage. What I don't agree with is modern Pure, who have never experienced Pangea, but buy into the stories of it having been a paradise that <i>those other werewolves</i> ruined for the rest of us. They kill their own kind over a millenia-old grudge, but it was not the modern Forsaken who killed Father Wolf, and the modern Pure never had a Pangea to lose. They hold innocent people responsible for the actions of their <i>shared</i> ancestors, just because they side with the Firstborn who say &quot;naw dog, I was there, and Pangea was not all it's cracked up to be. The First Pack did the right thing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T20:01:17-07:00","id":475246,"title":"","content":"I feel it is necessary to remind people that Dire Wolf was NOT opposed to the death of mother wolf. He was weak and could no longer sustain the hunt, and so it is only natural that he fell. His hatred comes form the loss of pangaea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T05:39:03-07:00","id":475655,"title":"","content":"As one from opposition of idea of Pure Tribes in the first place ( in 1ed corebook they were portrayed as werewolf terrorist, killing you without any real reason ) I must say that <b>Pure</b> supplement add to them depth and some reason. But still they feel largely brainwashed in gameline.<br /> <br /> You can agree with their ideology that Father Moon is capricious and mad parent that has his own agenda - the agenda that could not be in the best interest of Uratha race. You can understand Pure's need for rebuilding Pangaea as Paradise Lost that says they will be apex of food chain when the world returns to the previous ways. You can look as semi understanding when you hear they story about Pogrom that nearly wipe out Pure Tribes just after forming them by the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> But then you contrast in what Pure actually do on daily basis - they torture and brainwash new cubs or seeking converts from Tribes of Moon, degrading them. They strip their Auspices, making ritual scaring, only to being free from &quot;monstrous parent&quot; ( i.e. Luna ). They are under Spirits Lord thumbs, only to win the war they probably cannot, as they want extermination of ideas ( i.e. Tribes of Moon ) in Uratha society. And they treat humanity like garbage, only saying that werewolves are important, humans are only for reproduction. In the end, they are more animalistic Seers of Throne. Only the Seers are at least sympathetic in they way that they have individual positive marks. Pure are only self-deluded Father Wolf long dead corpse fanatics - at least how they are portrayed in books.<br /> <br /> I want to add them more human spin, just like was shown by one of users in previous Pure topics. In my POV, Pure are as continuing Mother Wolf linage as Forsaken - looking in to Spirit, taking care of humans relatives and friends. They just make tougher choices because they hate Luna and dream of restoration for Pangaea, so Auspice are their sacrifice in the way to &quot;fight the wrong mother&quot;. They are not slaves to their powerful Totems, rather partners in uneasy trust - not often, but there are story of Pure pack to overthrow the Totem that used them too much. And then all the ideology of them makes some sens - even converts from Forsaken are logical alternative. More of it, I see Fire-Touched as saying most &quot;we are also children of Father Wolf, but we are true to our ways and actions. See how we fulfill our own promises, Forsaken.&quot;<br /> <br /> With 2ED, I have even idea of Predator King NPC that has his 8 year old daughter living with him in their RV as his Physical Touchstone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T21:23:52-07:00","id":476618,"title":"","content":"I spent today working up new spins for the Pure packs as my 2ed game gets underway. They're less &quot;For the Evil&quot; that 1ED were because I fell in love with the idea someone on here mentioned that the Sundering happened because of the rise of mankind's first cities. In my canon, the Pure are the werewolves who disagreed with that change in humanity's outlook and try to crush it even to this day. It's less about the murder and more about the fallout. They're also very, very rough-drafty. I hope that they serve as inspiration for someone else. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Predator Kings </b>- This tribe throws off their human ancestry, becoming the monster in the woods. Applicants to the Predator Kings are welcomed from anywhere as long as the werewolf in question is completely on board with severing all ties to their human past and submit themselves to the Hunt and what they truly are now: a wolf-spirit. Predator Kings are fluent in the First Tongue as if all of their forms are Gauru due to their adherence to speaking it (and only it). Initiation rites where the applicant is forced to speak the Oath of Father Wolf in perfect clarity while being harried by Urshul wolves is common. The one exception to the tribe's open door policy on accepting new recruits is that the Uratha in question is never from a Wolf-Blooded line connected to the Iron Masters, or was an Iron Master. The Predator Kings see the Iron Masters as the architects of how Pangaea was lost and interactions between the two tribes always end up with someone dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fire-Touched</b> - The Fire-Touched remember an age where Gods stalked the tribes of humanity and the horrible truth lurked just beyond the campfires. Today, humans have lost touch with the divine and prays to dead gods, ignoring the true Spirit Lords that slumber deep within the Hisil. The Fire-Touched believe that given enough worship and essence even Father Wolf can be brought back and wish to spread this truth through fear and fervor. It was humanity's collective turn away from the Hunt that led to the weakened Father - if they can just be scared properly enough to understand why the Hunt was needed, maybe the essence will flow again. This tribe tends to allow - even encourage - their Spirit allies to Urge and Claim the Wolf-Blooded. The strong among them will awaken as Uratha and the rest will serve as fodder to further the tribe's goals.<br /> <br /> <b>Ivory Claws </b>- To be an Ivory Claw is to be born knowing that you carry the unenviable duty of being the heirs of Father Wolf. All Uratha are descendants of the Wolf - the Ivory Claws don't deny this - but the Pure are the inevitable choice for ushering the world into a new Pangaea and who better to lead them than the ivory Claws?. To this tribe, humanity is the key to unlocking the new era and tend to use humans as tools and fodder for their plans and machinations. The scary part is that the Ivory Claws wield humanity like the perfect weapon, adapting to it in a way that Father Wolf never could. However, the Ivory Claws believe that only their tribe is worthy of cultivating humans and tends to see any sort of interference from other supernaturals as reasons to turn humanity like a scythe against the offenders. The Forsaken are the worst of the lot; they have all the potential to stand alongside the Pure as the incinerators of Pangaea but instead the Forsaken bind themselves with silver chains to a Moon Goddess and work as her lapdogs. It's a shameful display and the Ivory Claws will force the Forsaken to see reason and truth, even if they have to flay the silver from their bodies one renown brand at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:11:08-07:00","id":479389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire-Touched[/B] - The Fire-Touched remember an age where Gods stalked the tribes of humanity and the horrible truth lurked just beyond the campfires. Today, humans have lost touch with the divine and prays to dead gods, ignoring the true Spirit Lords that slumber deep within the Hisil. The Fire-Touched believe that given enough worship and essence even Father Wolf can be brought back and wish to spread this truth through fear and fervor. It was humanity's collective turn away from the Hunt that led to the weakened Father - if they can just be scared properly enough to understand why the Hunt was needed, maybe the essence will flow again. This tribe tends to allow - even encourage - their Spirit allies to Urge and Claim the Wolf-Blooded. The strong among them will awaken as Uratha and the rest will serve as fodder to further the tribe's goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the ones i feel sympathetic about,even if just a bit,they are doing evil,terrorist acts,but in the end,at least part of their motivations is that <i>they want their dad back</i>,its not the kind of thing i can not sympathize with<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T21:39:49-07:00","id":479887,"title":"","content":"Because with the right kind of motivation, evil acts of terror are totally ok!<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T03:46:16-07:00","id":480050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=479887#post479887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because with the right kind of motivation, evil acts of terror are totally ok!<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The scariest sort of evil is the sort that stems from good intentions. But they're not sympathetic. Each of the three Pure tribes wants to bring back Father Wolf but it's not because they miss their Father - it's because when he was alive and Pangaea existed, Uratha ruled the roost. They want humanity back to being scattered, scared settlements that are easily controlled and culled. The Ivory Claws want to rule, the Predator Kings want to destroy, and the Fire Touched want to worship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T08:50:09-07:00","id":480279,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget, though, that the Pure are all special and everything. Most people in this world have no idea why they're here or what they want to do. They do. They have a mission, a reason for being here. They're not here by chance. They're here because they are the chosen ones.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:07:23-07:00","id":480289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure#post473605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hei guys,first things first,i must apologize for any grammar or spelling mistakes i may make,i'm from brazil,my english is not that good About The Pure. Do any of you Empathize with them?Or at Least feel a little sorry for them?Because i do. I'm not saying i think they are the good guys,or that what they do is right. they are monsters,but if you look at their story... They had a Home in Pangea,it was a paradise for them. They could whatever they pleased,hunt whatever they wanted,they were Happy.And they were with their father. And them,theyr brothers murdered their father and as a consequence,they lost their home,they lost everything. i dont know,maybe its just me,but i think i can see why they are angry,they lost their dad,they lost their home,no wonder they want payback</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hmm, let's have a history lesson...<br /> <br /> <br /> Father Wolf was getting weaker and wasn't able to do his job properly. Rather than be good little pups and help daddy out with the chores, they decide &quot;lets kill him and take his place!&quot;<br /> <br /> Mother Luna didn't care who was involved, she smote all of her children, even the innocent ones and demanded they try to repent for a crime neither they nor their ancestors committed.<br /> <br /> The death of Father Wolf shattered the world forever into something that it was never intended to be. Instead of harmony between spirit and flesh, there's more chaos than ever before.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yes, I can totally understand why the Pure would be quite pissed off at the Forsaken and Luna herself. Just because 3 (I think) of the first born didn't try to fight the 4 others, they deserve the same punishment as those who carried out the murder? No thought to the fact they were outnumbered, or maybe confident in Father Wolf's abilities? Remember at the time Father Wolf was one of the mightiest spirits in the world, actually being powerful enough to force spirits and mortals to get along together. Surely he could have handled the arrogant pups who decided to take him on, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-14-2015, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:12:16-07:00","id":480292,"title":"","content":"That's not a history lesson; that's an analysis of the Forsaken creation myth. <br /> <br /> A history lesson would be a critical look at the Brethren War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:18:31-07:00","id":480295,"title":"","content":"I don't even buy that the silver thing is a curse any more. It's a bane - precisely what <i>every other comparable entity</i> in the world of darkness has in some form. That's not something that was laid down by a judgemental goddess, it's a natural consequence of being part-spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:19:12-07:00","id":480297,"title":"","content":"Forgot to add that because of Mother Luna, the werewolves also became half flesh by being made into humans. Before that time, they were pure spirits and by that speculation they were immortal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, who the hell are &quot;mother wolf&quot; and &quot;father moon?&quot;<br /> <br /> Did the parents get a gender swap in 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-14-2015, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:21:45-07:00","id":480299,"title":"","content":"They got a &quot;they're goddamn spirits what do they even need genders for anyway?&quot; in 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:30:35-07:00","id":480301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480297#post480297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgot to add that because of Mother Luna, the werewolves also became half flesh by being made into humans. Before that time, they were pure spirits and by that evidence they were immortal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/incorrectweeping.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Werewolves have always been half-flesh by the common myth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When Pangaea was in full bloom, its beauty seduced the heart of the moon itself. Mother Luna \u2014 Amahan Iduth \u2014 grew enchanted with the world growing beneath her. <b>She took the form of a woman of flesh and descended to earth.</b> She walked among the jungles and swam in the seas. She was the most beautiful creature in the world, and she had countless suitors. The greatest and most valiant was Urfarah\u2026 and you know that name, don\u2019t you? He was Father Wolf.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Father Wolf loved Luna as she rode across the skies, and was overcome with joy and love when he encountered her walking through the borderlands between the spirit world and the physical. He was not alone in either of these sentiments. For her part, Luna found Father Wolf to be valiant and wise, strong and handsome, and she loved him in return. <b>They knew one another, and she gave him children of both spirit and flesh \u2014 the first werewolves.</b> Although she wore a human body, Luna gave birth to the first werewolves as a litter of nine pups, a sign of their future fate. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, who the hell are &quot;mother wolf&quot; and &quot;father moon?&quot;<br /> <br /> Did the parents get a gender swap in 2nd edition? </div> </div> </div>Yep. Spirits do not give a fuck about gender, especially not spirits that change their entire nature with their face on a near-daily basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:38:11-07:00","id":480319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480279#post480279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget, though, that the Pure are all special and everything. Most people in this world have no idea why they're here or what they want to do. They do. They have a mission, a reason for being here. They're not here by chance. They're here because they are the chosen ones.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is what makes them evil,they think they are the chosen people.that is their mission to murder innocents and destroy lives,They are werewolf ISIS.Werewolf al qaeda etc....<br /> i dont sympathize with the whole terrorist thing,but i do understand the feeling of being in the top of the world,and then lost what you cared for.<br /> And in the end,if i lost my father,i really dont know what i would too to bring him back,somethinks i think i might have acted like the pure in their situation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:42:33-07:00","id":480348,"title":"","content":"Their mission isn't to murder innocents, to be fair. Unless you consider the Forsaken innocents, which they most assuredly do not.<br /> <br /> It's easy to see why they do what they do, but that doesn't necessarily mean you think what they do is right or the right way to handle their situation. There can be a great difference between understanding why someone is doing something and thinking that's a good thing to do. This is, in part, what makes the Pure good antagonists for the Forsaken. <br /> <br /> Underneath all the bloodshed and zealotry and arrogance, they have a point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:47:51-07:00","id":480352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480348#post480348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their mission isn't to murder innocents, to be fair. Unless you consider the Forsaken innocents, which they most assuredly do not.<br /> <br /> It's easy to see why they do what they do, but that doesn't necessarily mean you think what they do is right or the right way to handle their situation. There can be a great difference between understanding why someone is doing something and thinking that's a good thing to do. This is, in part, what makes the Pure good antagonists for the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Underneath all the bloodshed and zealotry and arrogance, they have a point.</div> </div> </div> </div> If i was a badass wolf whom spent their entire day hunting and having a hell of a time hunting alone,or with my buddies.<br /> And then i' lost everything,and i found out that the people i used to hunt built a civilization for themselves,i would be mad<br /> &quot;<i>they used to be prey,and now they </i>RULE the world,who gave them the RIGHT?&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T09:59:58-07:00","id":480362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480301#post480301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/incorrectweeping.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Werewolves have always been half-flesh by the common myth.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Either that's from 2nd edition, or I need to read my books again. To be honest, I've only glanced through Werewolf, and found it much more complicated than vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for spirits being able to change gender... that means that theoretically, Wolf and Luna could have been lesbians. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-14-2015, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:04:53-07:00","id":480369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480362#post480362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what I read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you didn't read the <i>first account of the Sundering that was presented in the line.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After the death of Father Wolf, Luna cursed the Werewolves by taking away their powers for an unidentified period of time, turning them into humans. When she finally gave them back is when they were half &amp; half. </div> </div> </div>I've read the entirety of Werewolf 1e, including the book full of alternate takes on the werewolf creation myth.<br /> <br /> This happens in none of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Father Wolf and Mother Luna were both spirits, so why the hell would their children be half flesh? </div> </div> </div>Because they are <i>gods</i> and this is a <i>myth</i> where <i>the worlds of flesh and spirit were closer</i>.<br /> <br /> The normal rules are so far from mattering to that context that you can barely see them on a clear day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:15:35-07:00","id":480387,"title":"","content":"Hey now, the Quicksilver Children have an answer about why the Uratha are half-flesh. You should listen to them, nothing could possibly go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:17:58-07:00","id":480395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480348#post480348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Underneath all the bloodshed and zealotry and arrogance, they have a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's that point again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:19:10-07:00","id":480397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480348#post480348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their mission isn't to murder innocents, to be fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not their <i>mission</i>, no (unless you count some factions of the Predator Kings, who totally have it as part of their mission). It's still <i>what they do</i>, as demonstrated in the books time and time again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:21:48-07:00","id":480400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480395#post480395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's that point again?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's several. Mother Luna is an insane slave mistress. Father Wolf's death might have not been deserved. Why should werewolves spend their lives toiling against their own kind for the protection of mankind? Why should the Pure be punished for the actions of the Forsaken? Why should they have to live in an alien world because the Forsaken ruined their true home?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-14-2015, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:25:05-07:00","id":480404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480400#post480400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's several. Mother Luna is an insane slave mistress. Father Wolf's death might have not been deserved. Why should werewolves spend their lives toiling against their own kind for the protection of mankind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's the evidence for any of that? <br /> <br /> The Forsaken do what they do because if they don't, the world falls apart, bad things fuck up their territory and violate their people. Evidence for that can be gathered by, well, not hunting and waiting a little while. <br /> <br /> Do the Pure have any sort of evidence that proves their dogma?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:31:10-07:00","id":480413,"title":"","content":"Nope. The pure murder people to avenge a dude who might never have existed and reclaim a world they might never have lived in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:33:35-07:00","id":480414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480404#post480404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's the evidence for any of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Silver brands, the Oath of the Moon. Everyone knows Luna's insane. Is there any proof Father Wolf deserved to die? And the fact that the Forsaken duty has no end. When one werewolf dies at the hands of its enemies, another will pick up its slack. Forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Forsaken do what they do because if they don't, the world falls apart, bad things fuck up their territory and violate their people. Evidence for that can be gathered by, well, not hunting and waiting a little while. </div> </div> </div>Their people being whom? Humans? But werewolves are part spirit, why defend humans and kill spirits? Werewolves might even be a host. Why kill hosts and spirits? And even the Forsaken kill humans sometimes. Forsaken choose to work on the side of humanity because Luna tells them to. Pure don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> D<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">o the Pure have any sort of evidence that proves their dogma?</span> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Uratha experience on either side is going to be born out in faith. The Uratha have no evidence that Father Wolf wanted them to kill him, or deserved to die, or wanted them to serve Luna, or that Luna didn't poison Father Wolf and weaken him so that she could usurp control over the werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480413#post480413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The pure murder people to avenge a dude who might never have existed and reclaim a world they might never have lived in.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Forsaken work to redeem themselves to death for a sin they might never have committed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:38:15-07:00","id":480418,"title":"","content":"I've always got the feeling there's a large chunk of Forsaken who couldn't give two shits about redemption and just do what they need to to keep the world from going nuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:39:49-07:00","id":480420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480414#post480414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver brands, the Oath of the Moon. Everyone knows Luna's insane. Is there any proof Father Wolf deserved to die? And the fact that the Forsaken duty has no end. When one werewolf dies at the hands of its enemies, another will pick up its slack. Forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have to tell you that none of that is evidence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480414#post480414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Uratha experience on either side is going to be born out in faith. The Uratha have no evidence that Father Wolf wanted them to kill him, or deserved to die, or wanted them to serve Luna, or that Luna didn't poison Father Wolf and weaken him so that she could usurp control over the werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Forsaken cause isn't about faith, it's not even about pragmatism, it's about making a choice and sticking to it, even if it means suffering the consequences. The Forsaken aren't the good guys because their faith happens to be right, they're the good guys because they have the moral fortitude to try and keep their territory clean and their people safe, unlike the Pure. <br /> <br /> Or, to quote Ethan Skemp, the guy who developed two Werewolf games a very long time: <br /> <br /> <i>The price of freedom is eternal vigilance.<br /> <br /> That's what being Forsaken is about. It's about the hard duty of stepping up on the wall and staring out into the darkness so that the people sleeping behind you can be safe. It's about refusing the devil's bargain that the Pure accepted, gaining power and allies and unity at a terrible cost to your own freedom and to the freedom of anybody you care about unfortunate enough to be born human. That is unquestionably what I love about the psychology werewolves of both W:tA and W:tF, that hardcore loyalty, the fact that just maybe your fury is righteous, defending the right things for the right reasons. It all gets more complicated than that in play, but that kernel of heroism is what matters.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat? Eternal vigilance was just a catchphrase for them. Their enemy wasn't just outside the walls. And they weren't defending anything but their own damn sorry skins. They were dogs mutilating sheep and fighting other dogs, all the while telling themselves &quot;But hey, this will make us all the stronger when the wolves show up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'll take a World of Darkness. I'll go with player characters that are complicated and have done bad things and will do bad things. But at the core of it, there needs to be some flicker of sacrifice, something greater than the simple &quot;looking out for Number One for as long as I can.&quot; And that's why Werewolf is so dear to my heart \u2014 that was what it was about before I came on, and it'll be what people are doing with Werewolf maybe even after I'm dead. </i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:41:56-07:00","id":480423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480418#post480418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always got the feeling there's a large chunk of Forsaken who couldn't give two shits about redemption and just do what they need to to keep the world from going nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Redemption&quot; in what context? Did the Forsaken PCs kill a god from a myth? Did any of the Forsaken who are alive do so? <br /> <br /> The Forsaken aren't about redemption, they're about hard choices and stepping up for what's right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:44:10-07:00","id":480425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480420#post480420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have to tell you that none of that is evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know what brands are? They're marks of ownership.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Forsaken cause isn't about faith, it's not even about pragmatism, it's about making a choice and sticking to it, even if it means suffering the consequences. </div> </div> </div>Except the Pure make a choice and stick to it, even if it means suffering the consequences as well. In fact, in terms of stick-to-itness, considering the Pure convert the Forsaken far more than the other way around, it looks like the Pure are more willing to suffer the consequences of low harmony and service to powerful totems.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:51:51-07:00","id":480428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480425#post480425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you know what brands are? They're marks of ownership.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compare the totem bans of the Pure with those of the Forsaken - not just the tribal ones, also the ones on a pack level. Compare, also, the Forsaken rites with the Pure rites - which of them get to have more freedom? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480425#post480425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the Pure make a choice and stick to it, even if it means suffering the consequences as well. In fact, in terms of stick-to-itness, considering the Pure convert the Forsaken far more than the other way around, it looks like the Pure are more willing to suffer the consequences of low harmony and service to powerful totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not their choices. It's choices made by their totems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:52:43-07:00","id":480430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480423#post480423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Redemption&quot; in what context? Did the Forsaken PCs kill a god from a myth? Did any of the Forsaken who are alive do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are being punished as if they had, through the bane of silver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Forsaken aren't about redemption, they're about hard choices and stepping up for what's right. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf the Forsaken, first edition rule book, page 254, 'The Shadow Realm doesn\u2019t provide the answers to any of the great questions of creation, and the werewolves are seeking answers and a way to redeem themselves for the murder of Father Wolf. Is it any wonder that some seek solutions in the same faiths they turned to before their true nature asserted itself?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:53:55-07:00","id":480431,"title":"","content":"Funny thing about free will: It's a lot easier to give up than get back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:55:43-07:00","id":480433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480428#post480428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare the totem bans of the Pure with those of the Forsaken - not just the tribal ones, also the ones on a pack level. Compare, also, the Forsaken rites with the Pure rites - which of them get to have more freedom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Between the brands brought down by the Mother Goddess who the Forsaken swear an oath to and the brands the Pure place on themselves when they deem each other worthy? The ones that don't swear allegiance to a mad god probably offer more freedom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not their choices. It's choices made by their totems. </div> </div> </div>You mean like the Forsaken's completely unconditional choice to follow the Oath of the Moon or go mad and be burnt by the merest touch of silver?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:57:10-07:00","id":480450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480430#post480430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are being punished as if they had, through the bane of silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bane that, interestingly, affects the Pure more than it does the Forsaken. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:59:15-07:00","id":480461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480433#post480433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between the brands brought down by the Mother Goddess who the Forsaken swear an oath to and the brands the Pure place on themselves when they deem each other worthy? The ones that don't swear allegiance to a mad god probably offer more freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that as if there were any negative consequences to swearing an oath to the Moon; demonstrate what those are. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480433#post480433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean like the Forsaken's completely unconditional choice to follow the Oath of the Moon or go mad and be burnt by the merest touch of silver?</div> </div> </div> </div>To &quot;swear&quot; the oath, not to follow the oath. There are plenty of Forsaken who don't care all that much about the Oath. Silver still doesn't affect them as much as the Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T11:03:31-07:00","id":480469,"title":"","content":"If the bane of silver is a punishment who exactly did <i>every other spirit in existence </i>piss off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T11:23:23-07:00","id":480510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480461#post480461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that as if there were any negative consequences to swearing an oath to the Moon; demonstrate what those are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not being able to live a normal life because you're following a seven thousand year old Oath to serve the god of the moon. In addition you can't tell your loved ones what you are, lest you risk them being put on a hit list because nu bath githul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To &quot;swear&quot; the oath, not to follow the oath. There are plenty of Forsaken who don't care all that much about the Oath. Silver still doesn't affect them as much as the Pure. </div> </div> </div>Harmony is based on the precepts of the Oath of the Moon in first edition. Losing Harmony led to madness. Now it leads to bans. Silver affecting the Pure is evidence that Luna punishes those who don't serve her.<br /> <br /> With terms like good guys and referring to the Sabbat, you seem to be looking at this from a certain angle. Humanocentric, killing equals evil sort of thing. Can you appreciate that some people may be looking at werewolves and appreciating that they're just as much spirit as they are human? That perhaps not being human allows them to live outside the traditional humanocentric perspective that we as humans base morality on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480469#post480469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the bane of silver is a punishment who exactly did <i>every other spirit in existence </i>piss off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits have a bane naturally. Werewolves are not spirits, they are half spirit. In both core books, Mother Luna specifically made them vulnerable to silver.<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Forsaken, first edition, page 169, 'Legend holds that when Luna heard of the death of Father Wolf, she \ufb02ew into a rage and cursed every one of her wolf-sired children for the deed. Silver, the metal most sacred to Luna, began to burn her werewolf descendants with a touch.<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Forsaken, second edition, page 65, 'Luna saw what Wolf\u2019s offspring had done, and cursed them with madness and to burn at the touch of silver.'<br /> <br /> All signs point at them not having a bane before. This might be further evidence supporting them as shartha, who exist without banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-14-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T11:38:31-07:00","id":480518,"title":"","content":"I look forward to the fresh bout of discussion that the material of the Neolithic chapter of Dark Eras will bring to Werewolf <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T11:44:07-07:00","id":480525,"title":"","content":"Really looking forward to it, should certainly answer a lot of questions and raise a lot more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T12:23:35-07:00","id":480595,"title":"","content":"I'm just saying, a lot of legends attribute somewhat negative facts of existence to divine curses placed on one's ancestors. It doesn't mean they're <i>true</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T14:28:25-07:00","id":480711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480595#post480595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just saying, a lot of legends attribute somewhat negative facts of existence to divine curses placed on one's ancestors. It doesn't mean they're <i>true</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is one of the few things everyone seems to agree on in the myth. But once you start accepting that people have have lied to fit their history why would you only look at it from a point of view of the Pure lying to support their outlook, and not the Forsaken to support theirs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T15:02:36-07:00","id":480751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480414#post480414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Silver brands, the Oath of the Moon. Everyone knows Luna's insane. Is there any proof Father Wolf deserved to die? And the fact that the Forsaken duty has no end. When one werewolf dies at the hands of its enemies, another will pick up its slack. Forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Their people being whom? Humans? But werewolves are part spirit, why defend humans and kill spirits? Werewolves might even be a host. Why kill hosts and spirits? And even the Forsaken kill humans sometimes. Forsaken choose to work on the side of humanity because Luna tells them to. Pure don't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the Uratha experience on either side is going to be born out in faith. The Uratha have no evidence that Father Wolf wanted them to kill him, or deserved to die, or wanted them to serve Luna, or that Luna didn't poison Father Wolf and weaken him so that she could usurp control over the werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And the Forsaken work to redeem themselves to death for a sin they might never have committed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One thing that confused me is that in order for Luna to restore their Werewolf abilities, the Forsaken had to pledge to take up Father Wolf's duty and swear the Oath of the Moon... the Pure said fuck that, and yet they still become Werewolves. So what's Luna's game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Can she not strip them of their powers a second time, or does she use The Pure as a proxis to continue punishing her husband's killers? Or maybe she just acted quickly to capitalize on their confusion as to why they were undergoing the First Change after Luna said &quot;No!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-14-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T15:11:33-07:00","id":480756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480420#post480420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The Sabbat? Eternal vigilance was just a catchphrase for them. Their enemy wasn't just outside the walls. And they weren't defending anything but their own damn sorry skins. They were dogs mutilating sheep and fighting other dogs, all the while telling themselves &quot;But hey, this will make us all the stronger when the wolves show up.&quot;<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, the Sabbat had werewolf allies, didn't they? Pentex, the Black Spiral Dancers, and The Sabbat were all on good terms with each other. Or at least that's what I found out watching some introductory videos on youtube. After all, werewolves believed vampires were the walking wyrm, and the BSD serve the wyrm, so yeah. Makes sense they'd want to partner up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-14-2015, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T15:13:45-07:00","id":480759,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that werewolves do protect spirits from humans when necessary. It's just not often necessary, because spirits can handle puny mortals quite well on their own, thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T15:23:21-07:00","id":480806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480751#post480751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> One thing that confused me is that in order for Luna to restore their Werewolf abilities, the Forsaken had to pledge to take up Father Wolf's duty and swear the Oath of the Moon... the Pure said fuck that, and yet they still become Werewolves. So what's Luna's game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Can she not strip them of their powers a second time, or does she use The Pure as a proxis to continue punishing her husband's killers? Or maybe she just acted quickly to capitalize on their confusion as to why they were undergoing the First Change after Luna said &quot;No!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna never stripped the Uratha of their werewolf abilities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T15:29:27-07:00","id":480813,"title":"","content":"All Luna did was inflict a weakness against Silver on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T15:49:06-07:00","id":480826,"title":"","content":"<i>Allegedly </i>*is shot*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T15:58:34-07:00","id":480831,"title":"","content":"What if Luna's thing with the Forsaken is her blessing lessens the strength of Silver being all uratha's ban. Because the Pure never worship or interact with her, they still have the full effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:00:43-07:00","id":480834,"title":"","content":"I think that is indeed the general idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:24:40-07:00","id":480852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480751#post480751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that confused me is that in order for Luna to restore their Werewolf abilities, the Forsaken had to pledge to take up Father Wolf's duty and swear the Oath of the Moon... the Pure said fuck that, and yet they still become Werewolves. So what's Luna's game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Can she not strip them of their powers a second time, or does she use The Pure as a proxis to continue punishing her husband's killers? Or maybe she just acted quickly to capitalize on their confusion as to why they were undergoing the First Change after Luna said &amp;quot;No!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>She never stripped them of their powers, she just made them weak to silver. When the Forsaken swore the oath of the moon, she lessened that weakness somewhat (though not entirely) and sent Lunes to brand them with Renown for great deeds done in her name and teach them the Gifts of their Auspice. The oldest of the Pure never swore the oath and never recieved these blessings, so they are as weak to silver as ever, have no Auspice, and must brand each other with Renown using a special rite. New Pure recruits have to perform a different rite to remove their Auspice in order to join (because all post-Oath Werewolves start out Forsaken upon their first change) and in doing so they give up the ability to use Auspice Gifts and to gain renown from Lunes, and lose their partial resistance to silver.<br /> <br /> Or, at least, that's how the legend goes. We'll learn more when Dark Eras comes out, and probably be left with even more questions we haven't even thought to ask yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:26:13-07:00","id":480856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480826#post480826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Allegedly </i>*is shot*</div> </div> </div> </div>No need for shooting, it's an important point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:32:27-07:00","id":480859,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=475915#post475915\">There is a pack of Pure in one of the books</a> that is trying to come at Luna as an ally, not as a servant. They have a Lune magath totem, and friendly relations with other Lunes.<br /> <br /> Their bane has not been relieved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-14-2015, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T17:21:27-07:00","id":480942,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, they're still Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T18:25:47-07:00","id":480982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480852#post480852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She never stripped them of their powers, she just made them weak to silver. When the Forsaken swore the oath of the moon, she lessened that weakness somewhat (though not entirely) and sent Lunes to brand them with Renown for great deeds done in her name and teach them the Gifts of their Auspice. The oldest of the Pure never swore the oath and never recieved these blessings, so they are as weak to silver as ever, have no Auspice, and must brand each other with Renown using a special rite. New Pure recruits have to perform a different rite to remove their Auspice in order to join (because all post-Oath Werewolves start out Forsaken upon their first change) and in doing so they give up the ability to use Auspice Gifts and to gain renown from Lunes, and lose their partial resistance to silver.<br /> <br /> Or, at least, that's how the legend goes. We'll learn more when Dark Eras comes out, and probably be left with even more questions we haven't even thought to ask yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> How do the Ivory Claws recruit new members though if everybody starts as Forsaken? It was my understanding they are obsessed with purity and never allow &quot;Luna's weaklings&quot; to join them. They even have blood magic that can detect if anybody has ever served Luna... kind of no need for it if they're Forsaken by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T19:16:50-07:00","id":481032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480982#post480982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the Ivory Claws recruit new members though if everybody starts as Forsaken? It was my understanding they are obsessed with purity and never allow &quot;Luna's weaklings&quot; to join them. They even have blood magic that can detect if anybody has ever served Luna... kind of no need for it if they're Forsaken by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just how it works. When a werewolf first changes, the moon that's out becomes their Auspice. The Pure usually recruit new werewolves before they take the oath or join a tribe, if that's what you mean, but all werewolves start out with an Auspice, a Moon Gift, the capability of gaining Renown, and are slightly less harshly damaged by silver than the Pure are.. A rite is required to remove one's Auspice, and its associated benefits, and said rite is required to join any of the Pure tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T20:27:40-07:00","id":481067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480982#post480982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the Ivory Claws recruit new members though if everybody starts as Forsaken? It was my understanding they are obsessed with purity and never allow &quot;Luna's weaklings&quot; to join them. They even have blood magic that can detect if anybody has ever served Luna... kind of no need for it if they're Forsaken by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a rite* to prevent an auspice from setting at the First Change and the Ivory Claws keep very good genealogical records.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* That the rite literally involves being <i>held face-down in the dirt and covered with filth</i> should tell you something about how ironic the Anshega's chosen sobriquet is.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T20:52:40-07:00","id":481094,"title":"","content":"One thing I always liked about Book of Spirits is that it took time to specifically mention that 9 times out of 10 a spirit that could cross the gauntlet and claim a person doesn't because they have a natural fear that Werewolves will come and fuck their day up. For a non-Werewolf supplement it was enjoyable to see that Uratha are providing a valuable service that's pretty important. Even if the myths are are just lessons and parables they provide a good stepping stone to giving a character something to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T17:49:06-07:00","id":481766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=481067#post481067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a rite* to prevent an auspice from setting at the First Change and the Ivory Claws keep very good genealogical records.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* That the rite literally involves being <i>held face-down in the dirt and covered with filth</i> should tell you something about how ironic the Anshega's chosen sobriquet is.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>By filth he means stuff like piss and shit, too. Just to put stuff into perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T18:03:04-07:00","id":481792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=480982#post480982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the Ivory Claws recruit new members though if everybody starts as Forsaken? It was my understanding they are obsessed with purity and never allow &quot;Luna's weaklings&quot; to join them. They even have blood magic that can detect if anybody has ever served Luna... kind of no need for it if they're Forsaken by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't Forsaken by default. You aren't Forsaken until you join a Forsaken tribe. That's what the Ivory Claws have a beef with. Fire-Touched will recruit former Forsaken, but the Ivory Claws won't take anyone who has bended their knee to Luna. The auspices are a separate problem, which they have rites to address. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T21:39:17-07:00","id":481916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473605-question-about-the-pure?p=481792#post481792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't Forsaken by default. You aren't Forsaken until you join a Forsaken tribe. That's what the Ivory Claws have a beef with. Fire-Touched will recruit former Forsaken, but the Ivory Claws won't take anyone who has bended their knee to Luna. The auspices are a separate problem, which they have rites to address. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Right, sorry, that was a wording problem on my part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}